  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7},$ where $\\theta =m\u2220A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ opposite to $\u2220A.$ Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot 7 \\\\ AB & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}-(\\sqrt{13})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49-13} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
